{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_ca47a558a3c55faf98326760de021734","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Contract\n2\t\n3\tRun: 2026-08-05 · branch `feat/phase1-foundations` · prior contract archived at\n4\t`.loops/archive/contract-01d2954.md`\n5\t\n6\t## Goal\n7\t\n8\tThree deliverables:\n9\t\n10\t- **D1** — Stop the ADHD ruleset from loading twice per session. CLAUDE.md is the\n11\t  single source of truth; the plugin's always-on SessionStart injection goes away.\n12\t- **D2** — Document and prove out GPT-5.6 access through the already-configured\n13\t  HAIP gateway. No proxy, no install: `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` /\n14\t  `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` are already exported from `~/.zshenv`.\n15\t- **D3** — Audit CLAUDE.md against its own rule 8 (delete the harness), and fix\n16\t  the agent-tooling gaps found during this run.\n17\t\n18\t## Established facts (verified, do not re-litigate)\n19\t\n20\t- `/Users/devashar/.claude/CLAUDE.md` is a **symlink** to\n21\t  `loops/.claude/CLAUDE.md`. The repo file is the global instruction file.\n22\t- The ADHD ruleset loads twice: CLAUDE.md lines 99–156 (user's tuned ~35-line\n23\t  version), and the plugin SessionStart hook gated on\n24\t  `~/.claude/.i-have-adhd-always`, which emits the full 6848-byte SKILL.md body.\n25\t- A real completion **succeeds** against `gpt-5.6-terra-mantle` through HAIP on\n26\t  both `/v1/messages` (Anthropic shape) and `/v1/chat/completions` (OpenAI\n27\t  shape). Returned text `ok`.\n28\t- HAIP serves: `gpt-5.6-terra-mantle`, `gpt-5.6-luna-mantle`, gpt-5.5(-mantle,\n29\t  -nano), gpt-5.4(-mantle, -nano), gpt-5-mini; claude-opus-5, claude-opus-4-8,\n30\t  claude-opus-4-7, claude-opus-4-6, claude-sonnet-5, claude-haiku-4-5; Gemini\n31\t  3.x flash and flash-lite.\n32\t- HAIP does **not** serve `gpt-5.6-sol`. It does **not** serve `claude-fable-5`.\n33\t- Costs per 1M in/out: Luna $0.20/$1.20 · Terra $2/$12 · Sol $5/$30 ·\n34\t  Haiku 4.5 $1/$5. Luna is cheaper than Haiku.\n35\t- `agents/explorer.md` and `agents/planner.md` both declare\n36\t  `tools: Read, Grep, Glob` — no Bash, no Write. Recon and file-authoring tasks\n37\t  dispatched to them fail silently.\n38\t\n39\t## Constraints\n40\t\n41\t- D1 touches only: delete `/Users/devashar/.claude/.i-have-adhd-always`.\n42\t- D2 writes documentation and log artifacts only. It must never write the value\n43\t  of `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` or `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` into any repo file. No\n44\t  proxy, no new env file, no install step.\n45\t- D3 touches only `.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/agents/explorer.md`, and\n46\t  `.claude/agents/planner.md`.\n47\t- D4 touches only `.claude/agents/builder.md`, `.claude/agents/evaluator.md`,\n48\t  `.claude/agents/explorer.md`, and `.loops/haip-config.md`. It may write\n49\t  `.loops/haip-<role>-observed.log` artifacts.\n50\t- D4 may not change any agent's `model:` field unless that tier passed its\n51\t  observed tool-using run. A failed or unrun proof leaves the field untouched.\n52\t- CLAUDE.md lines 99–130 (the ADHD ruleset wording) stay byte-identical.\n53\t- No criterion may adopt `gpt-5.6-sol` as available, or treat \"top tier\" as\n54\t  decided.\n55\t- No criterion may mark a GPT-tier role reassignment done without an observed\n56\t  tool-using run.\n57\t- No backward-compat shims (CLAUDE.md engineering principles). Remove obsolete\n58\t  paths outright.\n59\t- All edits to CLAUDE.md must be reviewable as a `git diff`.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance criteria\n62\t\n63\t### D1 — stop double-injection (5)\n64\t\n65\t1. `test ! -e /Users/devashar/.claude/.i-have-adhd-always`\n66\t2. Both hook copies (`plugins/cache/...` and `plugins/marketplaces/...`), run\n67\t   directly with the flag absent, exit 0 and print 0 bytes.\n68\t3. `jq -e '.enabledPlugins[\"i-have-adhd@i-have-adhd\"] == true'` on\n69\t   `~/.claude/settings.json` — plugin stays installed so `/i-have-adhd` still\n70\t   works on demand.\n71\t4. `skills/i-have-adhd/SKILL.md` unmodified (sha256 matches pre-build snapshot),\n72\t   `disable-model-invocation: true` intact.\n73\t5. CLAUDE.md lines 99–130 byte-identical to pre-build snapshot.\n74\t\n75\t### D2 — HAIP-backed GPT-5.6 access (6)\n76\t\n77\t6. `.loops/haip-config.md` documents variable **names** (`ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`,\n78\t   `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`, sourced from `~/.zshenv`), a redacted host, and the\n79\t   full confirmed model list. States explicitly that `gpt-5.6-sol` is NOT\n80\t   served. Check: grep for each required token string.\n81\t7. Hard secret gate: `grep -rF \"$ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN\"` across the repo returns\n82\t   0 hits; `git diff` contains no token-shaped secret line.\n83\t8. `.loops/haip-probe-terra.log` and `.loops/haip-probe-luna.log` exist, each\n84\t   from an actually-executed call, non-empty, containing a non-error response\n85\t   body. Terra probed on both API shapes.\n86\t9. `## Tier mapping` section: luna and terra each mapped to a candidate role\n87\t   with its cost line; an explicit \"Opus remains orchestrator\" sentence; no\n88\t   reference to sol as available.\n89\t10. **Risk-1 gate.** Any role reassignment in criterion 9 has a matching\n90\t    `.loops/haip-<role>-observed.log` showing that agent, under the GPT tier,\n91\t    invoking its declared tools and completing the designated proof task\n92\t    (defined in D4, criterion 18) — distinct from the bare completion probe in 8.\n93\t    Missing this, the mapping entry must carry the literal marker\n94\t    `PROPOSED-NOT-VERIFIED`.\n95\t11. **Risk-2 gate.** `## Context window` section states either an executed,\n96\t    observed effective limit for a non-Anthropic model through HAIP, or the\n97\t    literal string `unverified — assume capped at 200k`.\n98\t\n99\t### D3 — trim CLAUDE.md + agent-tooling fix (6)\n100\t\n101\t12. `wc -l .claude/CLAUDE.md` is **≤ 130** (from 156). Every heading in\n102\t    criterion 13 must survive the trim.\n103\t13. These headings survive: `## The loop`, `## The nine rules`, `## Routing`,\n104\t    an `Output style` heading, an `Engineering principles` heading.\n105\t14. CLAUDE.md lines 99–130 byte-identical to pre-build snapshot.\n106\t15. `git diff --name-only` touches only the files named in Constraints.\n107\t16. `agents/explorer.md` gains `Bash` in its `tools:` frontmatter, OR its body\n108\t    gains an explicit sentence stating it cannot inspect binaries, run CLIs, or\n109\t    verify installed-tool behaviour, and that such recon goes elsewhere.\n110\t    `agents/planner.md` likewise gains `Write` or an explicit statement that it\n111\t    cannot persist files and must return content to the orchestrator.\n112\t17. Regression guard: `! grep -rq claude-fable-5 .claude/` — nothing may\n113\t    reference a model HAIP does not serve.\n114\t\n115\t### D4 — roster flip, proof-gated (4)\n116\t\n117\tTarget roster: **opus-5 orchestrates** (this session, never delegated) ·\n118\t**terra critiques** (evaluator) · **luna writes all code** (builder) ·\n119\t**haiku finds** (explorer). Each non-orchestrator reassignment is gated on its\n120\town observed run.\n121\t\n122\t18. **Proof task, defined.** For each candidate tier a real subagent run is\n123\t    executed and captured to `.loops/haip-<role>-observed.log`. The run is only\n124\t    a pass if the log shows the agent *invoking its declared tools*, not merely\n125\t    emitting text:\n126\t    - `builder`/luna — must Read an existing repo file, make one scoped Edit to\n127\t      a scratch file under `/tmp`, run one Bash command, and report the result.\n128\t      Log must evidence all three tool types.\n129\t    - `evaluator`/terra — must Read the contract, run the verify script via\n130\t      Bash, and return a numeric 0–1 score with at least one named gap. Log\n131\t      must evidence Read + Bash + a parsable score.\n132\t    A log containing only assistant prose, or a refusal, or a tool call with no\n133\t    result, is a FAIL for that tier.\n134\t19. `agents/builder.md` sets `model: gpt-5.6-luna-mantle` **iff** criterion 18's\n135\t    builder proof passed. Otherwise the file's `model:` is unchanged and\n136\t    `haip-config.md`'s mapping row carries `PROPOSED-NOT-VERIFIED`.\n137\t20. `agents/evaluator.md` sets `model: gpt-5.6-terra-mantle` **iff** criterion\n138\t    18's evaluator proof passed. Same fallback rule as 19.\n139\t21. `agents/explorer.md` keeps an explicitly stated model tier and, per\n140\t    criterion 16, either gains `Bash` or states it cannot do CLI recon. The\n141\t    luna-vs-haiku cost note ($0.20/$1.20 vs $1/$5) is recorded in\n142\t    `haip-config.md` as a decision with a stated reason either way.\n143\t\n144\t## Verify command\n145\t\n146\t`bash .loops/verify.sh` — created by the builder, containing:\n147\t\n148\t```bash\n149\tset -euo pipefail\n150\tcd /Users/devashar/Documents/DS/workspace/loops\n151\t\n152\t# D1\n153\ttest ! -e \"$HOME/.claude/.i-have-adhd-always\"\n154\tfor h in \"$HOME/.claude/plugins/cache/i-have-adhd/i-have-adhd/0.1.0/hooks/always-on.sh\" \\\n155\t         \"$HOME/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/i-have-adhd/hooks/always-on.sh\"; do\n156\t  [ -f \"$h\" ] || continue\n157\t  out=$(sh \"$h\"); [ -z \"$out\" ]\n158\tdone\n159\tjq -e '.enabledPlugins[\"i-have-adhd@i-have-adhd\"] == true' \"$HOME/.claude/settings.json\" >/dev/null\n160\t\n161\t# D2\n162\ttest -s .loops/haip-config.md\n163\tfor tok in gpt-5.6-terra-mantle gpt-5.6-luna-mantle gpt-5.6-sol \\\n164\t           '## Tier mapping' '## Context window'; do\n165\t  grep -q \"$tok\" .loops/haip-config.md\n166\tdone\n167\ttest -s .loops/haip-probe-terra.log\n168\ttest -s .loops/haip-probe-luna.log\n169\tif [ -n \"${ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN:-}\" ]; then\n170\t  ! grep -rqF \"$ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN\" . 2>/dev/null\n171\tfi\n172\t\n173\t# D3\n174\t! grep -rq claude-fable-5 .claude/\n175\tfor h in '## The loop' '## The nine rules' '## Routing' 'Output style' 'Engineering principles'; do\n176\t  grep -q \"$h\" .claude/CLAUDE.md\n177\tdone\n178\tgrep -qE 'Bash|cannot inspect binaries' .claude/agents/explorer.md\n179\tgrep -qE 'Write|cannot persist files' .claude/agents/planner.md\n180\twc -l .claude/CLAUDE.md\n181\t\n182\techo VERIFY_OK\n183\t```\n184\t\n185\tCriteria requiring evaluator judgement rather than the script: 4, 5, 10, 14, 15.\n186\t\n187\t## Out of scope\n188\t\n189\t- Patching the i-have-adhd plugin upstream or opening a PR.\n190\t- Any proxy that routes an Anthropic subscription OAuth token (violates\n191\t  Anthropic consumer terms).\n192\t- Requesting that platform add `gpt-5.6-sol` to HAIP (surfaced as a follow-up).\n193\t- Pushing, deploying, or publishing anything.\n194\t\n195\t## Resolved decisions (contract LOCKED 2026-08-05)\n196\t\n197\t- **Q1 → ≤130 lines**, all criterion-13 headings surviving. Criterion 12.\n198\t- **Q2 → proof task defined in criterion 18**, per-role, tool-invocation\n199\t  evidenced in the log. Prose-only logs fail.\n200\t- **Q3 → Terra accepted** as the top GPT tier available. Sol is recorded as a\n201\t  platform follow-up, not a blocker. This run proceeds.\n202\t\n203\tAmendment note: D4 (criteria 18–21) added at lock time to cover the requested\n204\troster flip — opus orchestrates, terra critiques, luna codes, haiku explores.\n205\tThe Risk-1 gate already in criterion 10 governs it; D4 makes the per-role\n206\toutcome explicit rather than leaving it to prose.\n207\t\n208\tKnown redundancy, deliberately kept: criteria 5 and 14 assert the same\n209\tbyte-identity on CLAUDE.md lines 99–130. Kept because they gate different\n210\tdeliverables (D1's hook removal vs D3's trim) and either could break it\n211\tindependently. Collapse only if a future run merges D1 and D3.\n212\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0fe4f34e-0e10-438b-b255-f62f98d7d6ab","uuid":"69f722ca-6f13-40af-b7b9-e16d54efd90d","timestamp":"2026-08-05T18:03:40.299Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/devashar/Documents/DS/workspace/loops/.loops/contract.md","content":"# Contract\n\nRun: 2026-08-05 · branch `feat/phase1-foundations` · prior contract archived at\n`.loops/archive/contract-01d2954.md`\n\n## Goal\n\nThree deliverables:\n\n- **D1** — Stop the ADHD ruleset from loading twice per session. CLAUDE.md is the\n  single source of truth; the plugin's always-on SessionStart injection goes away.\n- **D2** — Document and prove out GPT-5.6 access through the already-configured\n  HAIP gateway. No proxy, no install: `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` /\n  `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` are already exported from `~/.zshenv`.\n- **D3** — Audit CLAUDE.md against its own rule 8 (delete the harness), and fix\n  the agent-tooling gaps found during this run.\n\n## Established facts (verified, do not re-litigate)\n\n- `/Users/devashar/.claude/CLAUDE.md` is a **symlink** to\n  `loops/.claude/CLAUDE.md`. The repo file is the global instruction file.\n- The ADHD ruleset loads twice: CLAUDE.md lines 99–156 (user's tuned ~35-line\n  version), and the plugin SessionStart hook gated on\n  `~/.claude/.i-have-adhd-always`, which emits the full 6848-byte SKILL.md body.\n- A real completion **succeeds** against `gpt-5.6-terra-mantle` through HAIP on\n  both `/v1/messages` (Anthropic shape) and `/v1/chat/completions` (OpenAI\n  shape). Returned text `ok`.\n- HAIP serves: `gpt-5.6-terra-mantle`, `gpt-5.6-luna-mantle`, gpt-5.5(-mantle,\n  -nano), gpt-5.4(-mantle, -nano), gpt-5-mini; claude-opus-5, claude-opus-4-8,\n  claude-opus-4-7, claude-opus-4-6, claude-sonnet-5, claude-haiku-4-5; Gemini\n  3.x flash and flash-lite.\n- HAIP does **not** serve `gpt-5.6-sol`. It does **not** serve `claude-fable-5`.\n- Costs per 1M in/out: Luna $0.20/$1.20 · Terra $2/$12 · Sol $5/$30 ·\n  Haiku 4.5 $1/$5. Luna is cheaper than Haiku.\n- `agents/explorer.md` and `agents/planner.md` both declare\n  `tools: Read, Grep, Glob` — no Bash, no Write. Recon and file-authoring tasks\n  dispatched to them fail silently.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- D1 touches only: delete `/Users/devashar/.claude/.i-have-adhd-always`.\n- D2 writes documentation and log artifacts only. It must never write the value\n  of `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` or `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` into any repo file. No\n  proxy, no new env file, no install step.\n- D3 touches only `.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/agents/explorer.md`, and\n  `.claude/agents/planner.md`.\n- D4 touches only `.claude/agents/builder.md`, `.claude/agents/evaluator.md`,\n  `.claude/agents/explorer.md`, and `.loops/haip-config.md`. It may write\n  `.loops/haip-<role>-observed.log` artifacts.\n- D4 may not change any agent's `model:` field unless that tier passed its\n  observed tool-using run. A failed or unrun proof leaves the field untouched.\n- CLAUDE.md lines 99–130 (the ADHD ruleset wording) stay byte-identical.\n- No criterion may adopt `gpt-5.6-sol` as available, or treat \"top tier\" as\n  decided.\n- No criterion may mark a GPT-tier role reassignment done without an observed\n  tool-using run.\n- No backward-compat shims (CLAUDE.md engineering principles). Remove obsolete\n  paths outright.\n- All edits to CLAUDE.md must be reviewable as a `git diff`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n### D1 — stop double-injection (5)\n\n1. `test ! -e /Users/devashar/.claude/.i-have-adhd-always`\n2. Both hook copies (`plugins/cache/...` and `plugins/marketplaces/...`), run\n   directly with the flag absent, exit 0 and print 0 bytes.\n3. `jq -e '.enabledPlugins[\"i-have-adhd@i-have-adhd\"] == true'` on\n   `~/.claude/settings.json` — plugin stays installed so `/i-have-adhd` still\n   works on demand.\n4. `skills/i-have-adhd/SKILL.md` unmodified (sha256 matches pre-build snapshot),\n   `disable-model-invocation: true` intact.\n5. CLAUDE.md lines 99–130 byte-identical to pre-build snapshot.\n\n### D2 — HAIP-backed GPT-5.6 access (6)\n\n6. `.loops/haip-config.md` documents variable **names** (`ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`,\n   `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`, sourced from `~/.zshenv`), a redacted host, and the\n   full confirmed model list. States explicitly that `gpt-5.6-sol` is NOT\n   served. Check: grep for each required token string.\n7. Hard secret gate: `grep -rF \"$ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN\"` across the repo returns\n   0 hits; `git diff` contains no token-shaped secret line.\n8. `.loops/haip-probe-terra.log` and `.loops/haip-probe-luna.log` exist, each\n   from an actually-executed call, non-empty, containing a non-error response\n   body. Terra probed on both API shapes.\n9. `## Tier mapping` section: luna and terra each mapped to a candidate role\n   with its cost line; an explicit \"Opus remains orchestrator\" sentence; no\n   reference to sol as available.\n10. **Risk-1 gate.** Any role reassignment in criterion 9 has a matching\n    `.loops/haip-<role>-observed.log` showing that agent, under the GPT tier,\n    invoking its declared tools and completing the designated proof task\n    (defined in D4, criterion 18) — distinct from the bare completion probe in 8.\n    Missing this, the mapping entry must carry the literal marker\n    `PROPOSED-NOT-VERIFIED`.\n11. **Risk-2 gate.** `## Context window` section states either an executed,\n    observed effective limit for a non-Anthropic model through HAIP, or the\n    literal string `unverified — assume capped at 200k`.\n\n### D3 — trim CLAUDE.md + agent-tooling fix (6)\n\n12. `wc -l .claude/CLAUDE.md` is **≤ 130** (from 156). Every heading in\n    criterion 13 must survive the trim.\n13. These headings survive: `## The loop`, `## The nine rules`, `## Routing`,\n    an `Output style` heading, an `Engineering principles` heading.\n14. CLAUDE.md lines 99–130 byte-identical to pre-build snapshot.\n15. `git diff --name-only` touches only the files named in Constraints.\n16. `agents/explorer.md` gains `Bash` in its `tools:` frontmatter, OR its body\n    gains an explicit sentence stating it cannot inspect binaries, run CLIs, or\n    verify installed-tool behaviour, and that such recon goes elsewhere.\n    `agents/planner.md` likewise gains `Write` or an explicit statement that it\n    cannot persist files and must return content to the orchestrator.\n17. Regression guard: `! grep -rq claude-fable-5 .claude/` — nothing may\n    reference a model HAIP does not serve.\n\n### D4 — roster flip, proof-gated (4)\n\nTarget roster: **opus-5 orchestrates** (this session, never delegated) ·\n**terra critiques** (evaluator) · **luna writes all code** (builder) ·\n**haiku finds** (explorer). Each non-orchestrator reassignment is gated on its\nown observed run.\n\n18. **Proof task, defined.** For each candidate tier a real subagent run is\n    executed and captured to `.loops/haip-<role>-observed.log`. The run is only\n    a pass if the log shows the agent *invoking its declared tools*, not merely\n    emitting text:\n    - `builder`/luna — must Read an existing repo file, make one scoped Edit to\n      a scratch file under `/tmp`, run one Bash command, and report the result.\n      Log must evidence all three tool types.\n    - `evaluator`/terra — must Read the contract, run the verify script via\n      Bash, and return a numeric 0–1 score with at least one named gap. Log\n      must evidence Read + Bash + a parsable score.\n    A log containing only assistant prose, or a refusal, or a tool call with no\n    result, is a FAIL for that tier.\n19. `agents/builder.md` sets `model: gpt-5.6-luna-mantle` **iff** criterion 18's\n    builder proof passed. Otherwise the file's `model:` is unchanged and\n    `haip-config.md`'s mapping row carries `PROPOSED-NOT-VERIFIED`.\n20. `agents/evaluator.md` sets `model: gpt-5.6-terra-mantle` **iff** criterion\n    18's evaluator proof passed. Same fallback rule as 19.\n21. `agents/explorer.md` keeps an explicitly stated model tier and, per\n    criterion 16, either gains `Bash` or states it cannot do CLI recon. The\n    luna-vs-haiku cost note ($0.20/$1.20 vs $1/$5) is recorded in\n    `haip-config.md` as a decision with a stated reason either way.\n\n## Verify command\n\n`bash .loops/verify.sh` — created by the builder, containing:\n\n```bash\nset -euo pipefail\ncd /Users/devashar/Documents/DS/workspace/loops\n\n# D1\ntest ! -e \"$HOME/.claude/.i-have-adhd-always\"\nfor h in \"$HOME/.claude/plugins/cache/i-have-adhd/i-have-adhd/0.1.0/hooks/always-on.sh\" \\\n         \"$HOME/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/i-have-adhd/hooks/always-on.sh\"; do\n  [ -f \"$h\" ] || continue\n  out=$(sh \"$h\"); [ -z \"$out\" ]\ndone\njq -e '.enabledPlugins[\"i-have-adhd@i-have-adhd\"] == true' \"$HOME/.claude/settings.json\" >/dev/null\n\n# D2\ntest -s .loops/haip-config.md\nfor tok in gpt-5.6-terra-mantle gpt-5.6-luna-mantle gpt-5.6-sol \\\n           '## Tier mapping' '## Context window'; do\n  grep -q \"$tok\" .loops/haip-config.md\ndone\ntest -s .loops/haip-probe-terra.log\ntest -s .loops/haip-probe-luna.log\nif [ -n \"${ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN:-}\" ]; then\n  ! grep -rqF \"$ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN\" . 2>/dev/null\nfi\n\n# D3\n! grep -rq claude-fable-5 .claude/\nfor h in '## The loop' '## The nine rules' '## Routing' 'Output style' 'Engineering principles'; do\n  grep -q \"$h\" .claude/CLAUDE.md\ndone\ngrep -qE 'Bash|cannot inspect binaries' .claude/agents/explorer.md\ngrep -qE 'Write|cannot persist files' .claude/agents/planner.md\nwc -l .claude/CLAUDE.md\n\necho VERIFY_OK\n```\n\nCriteria requiring evaluator judgement rather than the script: 4, 5, 10, 14, 15.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Patching the i-have-adhd plugin upstream or opening a PR.\n- Any proxy that routes an Anthropic subscription OAuth token (violates\n  Anthropic consumer terms).\n- Requesting that platform add `gpt-5.6-sol` to HAIP (surfaced as a follow-up).\n- Pushing, deploying, or publishing anything.\n\n## Resolved decisions (contract LOCKED 2026-08-05)\n\n- **Q1 → ≤130 lines**, all criterion-13 headings surviving. Criterion 12.\n- **Q2 → proof task defined in criterion 18**, per-role, tool-invocation\n  evidenced in the log. Prose-only logs fail.\n- **Q3 → Terra accepted** as the top GPT tier available. Sol is recorded as a\n  platform follow-up, not a blocker. This run proceeds.\n\nAmendment note: D4 (criteria 18–21) added at lock time to cover the requested\nroster flip — opus orchestrates, terra critiques, luna codes, haiku explores.\nThe Risk-1 gate already in criterion 10 governs it; D4 makes the per-role\noutcome explicit rather than leaving it to prose.\n\nKnown redundancy, deliberately kept: criteria 5 and 14 assert the same\nbyte-identity on CLAUDE.md lines 99–130. Kept because they gate different\ndeliverables (D1's hook removal vs D3's trim) and either could break it\nindependently. Collapse only if a future run merges D1 and D3.\n","numLines":212,"startLine":1,"totalLines":212}}}
